            <p align="justify">
                Any claim, dispute or issues arising out of or in connection with this Contract, including any question regarding its existence, validity, interpretation or the
                enforcement, breach or termination thereof, shall, at the first instance, be settled by the Parties by mutual negotiations. If such claim, dispute or issues
                cannot be resolved by mutual negotiations within thirty (30) days from notice by either party of the existence of such claim, dispute or issue, the same shall
                be finally resolved by arbitration in the Philippines in accordance with the Arbitration Rules of the Philippine Dispute Resolution Center, Inc. ("PDRCI"), in
                force at the time of the commencement of arbitration. The appointing authority shall be the PDRCI. The arbitral tribunal shall be composed of three (3)
                arbitrators. Each party shall appoint one (1) arbitrator and the first two arbitrators shall appoint the third arbitrator, who shall be the chairman of the
                Tribunal. The place of arbitration is the Philippines and the venue of the hearings shall be in Manila, Philippines. The language to be used in the arbitral
